  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"2.6.5\"\n\npackage:\n  name: onionshare-cli\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/o/onionshare_cli/onionshare_cli-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: 6280e93307e5b8e78df5c23b346156d3cd3b8cb831e920ae33c3bb0edaf80ba2\n    patches:\n      - patches/0001-relax-dependency-pins.patch\n  # Neither the sdist nor the wheel ships a license file.\n  - url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/onionshare/onionshare/v${{ version }}/LICENSE.txt\n    sha256: 00209f6e6b6efaba0d150005ab108364bfeef6418345410835d725623661da4f\n    file_name: LICENSE.txt\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: python -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n  python:\n    entry_points:\n      - onionshare-cli = onionshare_cli:main\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - pip\n    - poetry-core\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - click\n    - colorama\n    - eventlet\n    - flask 3.1.*\n    - flask-compress >=1.24,<2\n    - flask-socketio >=5.6,<6\n    - gevent >=26.5.0\n    - gevent-websocket\n    - packaging >=24\n    - psutil\n    - pynacl >=1.6.2,<2\n    - pysocks\n    - qrcode >=7.4.2\n    - requests >=2.32.3\n    - stem >=1.8.0\n    - unidecode\n    - urllib3 >=2.7,<3\n    - waitress >=3.0.1,<4\n    - werkzeug 3.1.*\n    - tor\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - onionshare_cli\n        - onionshare_cli.web\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n      # conda-forge's stem 1.8.0 ships `Platform: UNKNOWN` in its metadata,\n      # which recent pip versions report as \"not supported on this platform\".\n      pip_check: false\n  - script:\n      - onionshare-cli --help\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://onionshare.org/\n  repository: https://github.com/onionshare/onionshare\n  documentation: https://docs.onionshare.org/\n  license: GPL-3.0-or-later\n  license_file: LICENSE.txt\n  summary: Securely and anonymously share files, host websites, and chat with friends using the Tor network\n  description: |\n    OnionShare is an open source tool that lets you securely and anonymously\n    share files, host websites, and chat with friends using the Tor network.\n\n    It works by starting a web server, making it accessible as a Tor onion\n    service, and generating an unguessable web address so others can download\n    files from you, or upload files to you. It does not require setting up a\n    separate server or using a third party file-sharing service.\n\n    This is the command line interface. The Qt desktop application is not\n    packaged yet.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - pavelzw\n",
